tt-local-generator (0.19.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Pipeline Studio Phase 2b-3 — "wing it". The composer's add-a-step area now has
    a free-form "describe the next step in your own words" box: type something
    like "set it to a slow piano and read it aloud" and it's mapped to a real,
    kind-safe pipeline step (a capability + params) and inserted. LLM-assisted via
    whatever chat model is running (ideally the always-on CPU prompt server),
    constrained to the live capabilities that can consume the current step's
    output, with a deterministic heuristic fallback when no model is up or the
    model misbehaves — so it never fails hard. New app/wingit.py (pure mapper with
    lenient JSON parsing + fallback; runs off the main thread, result applied via
    GLib.idle_add). This completes the free-form composer.

