tt-local-generator (0.14.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * pipeline: backend server-switching in app/pipeline_engine.py. Before each
    node runs, the engine maps its class_type + model to a backend
    (_backend_for): FLUX/SDXL for TTLGTextToImage, SkyReels/Wan/Mochi for
    TTLGImageToVideo, the artgen LLM (:8002) for TTLGGenerateText and LLM-backed
    TTLGArtgenGenerate, chips-free (stop+reset, no start) for TTLGAnimateDiff,
    and None (no switch) for CPU-only nodes. When the required backend differs
    from the active one it stops containers, resets the boards (only when
    switching from a prior backend), and starts the new server — mirroring
    bin/run_worlds_fair.sh. This gates the Milestone-1 QB2 run of the 1964 spec,
    which needs FLUX, SkyReels, and a 70B LLM to take turns on the hardware.
    Artgen start keys are derived from the model string; an unmappable model
    falls back to detecting an already-running LLM and only starting a default
    if none is up.
  * pipeline: --dry-run now emits intended-switch log lines but performs NO
    docker/tt-smi/tt-ctl calls, keeping CI 100% hardware-free.
  * pipeline: handler exceptions on optional nodes (per
    workflow_compat.COMPATIBILITY_MAP) are logged and skipped so the run
    continues; required nodes still fail-fast.
  * pipeline: TTLGArtgenGenerate dry-run output keys now mirror the real path
    (text only for text exts, png_path only for raster exts).
  * artgen: ArtGenerator gains a uses_llm flag (default True) so purely
    algorithmic plugin generators can opt out of LLM backend-switching.

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Sat, 11 Jul 2026 06:14:37 -0700

tt-local-generator (0.13.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * pipeline: real generic execution engine (app/pipeline_engine.py) replacing
    the run_workflow.sh stub, which ignored the spec and ran a hardcoded
    1964-World's-Fair sequence with unsubstituted placeholders. The engine loads
    any ComfyUI-API-v1 spec, topologically orders nodes by wire dependencies
    (resolving wires nested inside lists/dicts, e.g. playlist artifacts), and
    dispatches each class_type to a handler; emits the NODE:/LOG:/PLAYLIST:
    signals pipeline_runner.py parses. run_workflow.sh is now a thin shim over it.
    --dry-run runs the whole graph offline; proven on the 1964 World's Fair spec.
  * pipeline: TTLGArtgenGenerate (generic artgen-plugin node) and TTLGAnimateDiff
    nodes, registered in workflow_compat with an artgen-plugin-name check.
  * animatediff: CLI parity — tt-ctl artgen animatediff now forwards every
    run_subprocess parameter it previously dropped (multichip mode, per-chip
    prompts, seed spread, ramps, stitch order, lightning, chain, motion adapter),
    and correctly unpacks check_hardware()'s chip count so multi-chip engages
    from the CLI (previously it silently ran single-chip / crashed on hardware).
  * animatediff: prompt travel — schedule different prompts across the frame
    timeline (--prompt-schedule FRAME:PROMPT) for morphing content, via a new
    per-frame interpolated-conditioning path in tt-animatediff (sister project,
    re-released for this). Generalises multi-chip Remix's per-chip prompts onto
    the time axis. (Not yet supported in Coherent mode — warns and ignores.)
  * animatediff: seamless-loop crossfade (--loop seamless) — blends the tail
    frames into the head so GIFs loop without a seam; atomic save (temp +
    os.replace) so a failed post-process never corrupts the base GIF.

