tt-local-generator (0.3.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * artgen: add AnimateDiff Blackhole generator — direct TTNN UNet runner via
    generate_blackhole_v2.py, requires ~/tt-metal python_env and
    ~/tt-scratchpad/tt-animatediff (developer scratchpad path, not packaged).
    Gracefully degrades with an informative error when prerequisites are absent.
  * Watch mode: animated GIFs now loop correctly — GIF frames are decoded via
    GdkPixbuf.PixbufAnimation and driven by per-frame delay timers.  The GIF
    timer lifecycle is separated from slideshow timers so it survives
    _start_timers() / _stop_timers() restarts without being killed.
  * Watch mode: rich rendering for palette, verse, and ANSI text artgen records.
    Palette JSON renders as full-screen color swatch strip with name and lore;
    verse/freeform text renders as large centered italic text on dark canvas;
    ANSI art renders via existing HTML pipeline.  Plain Gtk.TextBuffer fallback
    is now only for unknown types.
  * Fix Playlist toolbar button on GTK 4.14: Gtk.MenuButton uses
    gtk_popover_popup() internally (not gtk_widget_show()), so the deprecated
    GtkWidget::show signal never fires.  Switched to notify::visible with a
    get_visible() guard — popover now populates reliably on every GTK 4.x.
  * setup_vendor.sh: auto-configure vendor/tt-inference-server/.env on fresh
    clone — detects HF_TOKEN from environment variables and credential files,
    prompts interactively when stdin is a terminal, generates a cryptographically
    random JWT_SECRET via openssl rand.  No-ops if .env already present.
  * postinst: generate vendor .env secrets automatically — JWT_SECRET is now
    randomised with openssl rand instead of defaulting to a static string;
    HF_TOKEN is sourced from the installing user's huggingface credential files
    when available.  Removes the manual "edit .env" step from the checklist.

